# Keep line endings out of the diff and out of cross-platform breakage.
#
# A repository that claims to work on Windows, Linux and macOS must not store the
# line endings of the machine that happened to commit first. Text is stored with LF
# and checked out with LF; the two Windows-only script formats need CRLF or the
# shell refuses to run them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary formats must never be normalised.
*.docx binary
*.doc binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.xlsx binary
